      "writtenOn": "2026-06-03T13:35:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This doesn\u0027t seem very efficient. Since we don\u0027t expose any way to enable/disable implicit animations on a per-layer basis, maybe you could just add a global flag somewhere that we test alongside the per-layer flag? Hell, maybe this could be a magic property of the current transaction? (Not sure if that one makes sense given the nested blocks thing… ah, could we use the nested block count as the flag?)",
      "revId": "0095f8866dce6abf0108d25880f23618ef0e4b17",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2d12f254_c091dd1e",
        "filename": "src/frameworks/uikit/ui_view.rs",
        "patchSetId": 53
      },
      "lineNbr": 244,
      "author": {
        "id": 1021822
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-06T15:48:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure that would do. CALayer use implicit animations by default, however, layers used by UIView\u0027s don\u0027t, and only have them enabled when there\u0027s an active UIView animation block active (not CATransaction). Using the UIView animation block count as a flag in CALayer would be mixing two different realms.",
      "parentUuid": "fe92a31f_fee6fa7a",
      "revId": "0095f8866dce6abf0108d25880f23618ef0e4b17",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9f528afe_6c2c7b8d",
        "filename": "src/frameworks/uikit/ui_view.rs",
        "patchSetId": 53
      },
      "lineNbr": 244,
      "author": {
        "id": 1021820
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-07T23:01:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, as a practical matter, `UIView`s are the only actual users of `set_use_implicit_animations(…, false)`, right? It is indeed unclean, but I feel like individually modifying the state of all UIViews with an O(n) loop is worse.",
      "parentUuid": "2d12f254_c091dd1e",
      "revId": "0095f8866dce6abf0108d25880f23618ef0e4b17",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1505dab7_466c91d0",
        "filename": "src/frameworks/uikit/ui_view.rs",
        "patchSetId": 53
      },
      "lineNbr": 244,
      "author": {
        "id": 1021820
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-07T23:07:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A cute way to make this conceptually cleaner would be to ask the layer delegate (which is the view if it was created by a view) whether implicit animations are enabled. After all, that\u0027s how disabling/enabling implicit animations *presumably* works in real iOS (I suspect `CALayerDelegate`\u0027s `actionForLayer:forKey:` is involved).\n\nBut adding a method call to an optional special touchHLE private selector on the delegate feels like… a bit much. I would suggest maybe just having a function like `uikit::is_implicit_animation_enabled(env, layer)` (and it could check if `layer` belongs to a `UIView`?)",
      "parentUuid": "9f528afe_6c2c7b8d",
      "revId": "0095f8866dce6abf0108d25880f23618ef0e4b17",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
